THOUGHT: The NullAway error is due to unboxing a potentially null Integer from the map (`countForResult == 1` and `countForResult - 1`). I should make the code robust to a null value by treating a missing entry as 0 and avoiding unboxing without a null check. I’ll update `remove()` so that if `countForResult` is null or 1, it removes the entry; otherwise it safely decrements using a primitive. Then I’ll run the Gradle compile to confirm the NullAway error count decreases by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/glide && sed -i '27,33c\    Integer countForResult = bitmapsPerType.get(result);
    int count = countForResult == null ? 0 : countForResult;
    if (count <= 1) {
      bitmapsPerType.remove(result);
      keyList.remove(keyIndex);
    } else {
      bitmapsPerType.put(result, count - 1);
    }' library/src/main/java/com/bumptech/glide/load/engine/prefill/PreFillQueue.java && ./gradlew library:compileDebugJavaWithJavac -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway:.*errors" -n new_build_output.log || tail -n 80 new_build_output.log
```

